#991 item 3 is answered: yes, stream-json's collected text joined both attempts after a mid-stream retry. I fixed it and committed as ea02d62d. Build, the full cargo test run, clippy with -D warnings and fmt --check all pass. I haven't pushed; that's left to the loop.

What I measured. The stream-json event loop never handled the start-of-message or retry events. With a test stream where attempt 1 sends PARTIAL_, then a retry, then attempt 2 sends PONG, the returned outcome held "PARTIAL_PONG" in both its full text and its text-since-last-tool. It now holds "PONG".

Who reads it. Nothing in production, for now. Both stream-json callers in src/main.rs only check whether there was an API error. So strictly this is the plan's case (b), "joins but nothing reads it". I fixed it instead of deleting the buffer because:
• the outcome is documented as the same one the normal text path returns;
• an existing test (#808) already checks this path's text, so deleting the buffer would have meant weakening that test.

The NDJSON output itself is unchanged. Consumers still see both attempts, with the retry event between them.

The fix. The existing truncation from the text path (#989) is now one helper, drop_dying_attempt in src/prompt/retry_after_partial.rs. Both loops call it, and it cuts only at character boundaries, never inside a multi-byte character.

Tests (src/prompt/stream_json_retry_tests.rs, all comparing full strings):
• the retry case gives PONG only;
• an earlier message is kept while a dying multi-byte attempt is dropped;
• with no retry, the result is PARTIAL_PONG, same as before;
• a retry before any text drops nothing.

I also broke the fix on purpose (marked NEUTERED) as one command. Exactly the two retry tests failed, by name. After restoring it, all four pass and no marker is left.

Files touched: src/prompt.rs, src/prompt/retry_after_partial.rs and the new test file. src/prompt.rs grew from 3912 to 3924 lines. That only triggers the size check's warning, which doesn't fail the build; the file was already 3 lines past its recorded size.

I posted the outcome, the measured values and the sha on #991, and noted that items 4a and 4b are still open.
